# TypeScript/JS sources are always text.
#
# `design-system/serializer.ts` carried a literal NUL byte (a delimiter written as
# a raw byte rather than an escape) until 0.2.9, and git therefore classified the
# whole file as binary: its diffs rendered as `Bin <n> -> <m> bytes` with no
# reviewable content, and grep skipped it silently. The byte is gone, but the
# next one should not be able to cost a reviewer a diff.
#
# 0.2.13: it happened again (`bin/c4s/delegate.ts`), because `text` alone could
# never have prevented it — that attribute governs end-of-line normalization and
# has no bearing on binary DETECTION. `diff` is the one that does: it tells git
# to diff a matching path as text whatever its bytes look like, and it applies
# retroactively, so a commit that already introduced a NUL stays reviewable.
# `tests/integration/architecture/source-bytes.test.ts` is the other half —
# `diff` keeps the review readable, the gate keeps the byte out.
*.ts  text diff
*.tsx text diff
*.js  text diff
*.jsx text diff
*.mjs text diff
*.cjs text diff
*.json text
*.md  text
